"""Explicit opt-in inline SDN grammar candidate; not imported by std.sdn.

Import this module and pass resource limits to request the shared grammar VM.
The standard std.sdn.parse / parse_file functions retain the legacy route.
Unsupported input returns Err; this facade never falls back to that route.
Use sdn_inline_parse_checked_v2 for phase/code and UTF-8 byte spans. A start
of -1 explicitly means no trusted position is available for that failure.
"""
use std.common.sdn.structural_inline_candidate_v2.{SdnInlineCandidateV2, SdnInlineIssueV2, sdn_inline_parse_candidate_v2, sdn_inline_parse_checked_v2}
use std.common.structural.parse.program_v1.{ParseProgramLimitsV1}

export SdnInlineCandidateV2, SdnInlineIssueV2, sdn_inline_parse_candidate_v2, sdn_inline_parse_checked_v2, ParseProgramLimitsV1
